1	box	You manage to carefully clamber down.
0	section	Attempting to pick up the coins
1	box	As soon as you touch the coins you hear the grinding sound of bones against stone as you see skeletons and zombies rising up out of the ground. The coins turn to dust in your hands.
1	line	Undead one	Prepare to go to the other side!
1	line	Undead one	Rahhhhh! OOoohhhhhh!
0	section	Open Tomb doors before placing bones
1	box	This door is completely sealed, it is very ornately carved.
0	section	Search Tomb doors
0	section	No bones put in
1	box	The door is ornately carved with depictions of skeletal warriors. You notice that some of the skeletal warriors depictions are not complete.Instead, there are recesses where some of the bones should be. There are three recesses.
1	action	end
0	section	One bone put in
1	box	The door is ornately carved with depictions of skeletal warriors. You notice that some of the skeletal warriors depictions are not complete.Instead, there are recesses where some of the bones should be. There are two recesses.
1	action	end
0	section	Two bones put in
1	box	The door is ornately carved with depictions of skeletal warriors. You notice that some of the skeletal warriors depictions are not complete.Instead, there are recesses where some of the bones should be. There is one recess.
1	action	end
0	section	Three bones put in
1	box	The door is ornately carved with depictions of skeletal warriors. All the skeletons are complete. It looks as if you walk through this door.
1	action	end
0	section	Using bones on Tomb doors
1	cond	If this is the first bone:
2	box	You carefully place a bone in the door...
2	box	You place the bone into the skeletal door and it fits. There are two recesses left now.
2	box	You fit the bone into the recess.
1	cond	If this is the second bone:
2	box	You carefully place another bone in the door...
2	box	You place the bone into the skeletal door and it fits. There is just one recess left now.
2	box	You fit the bone into the recess.
1	cond	If this is the third bone:
2	box	You carefully place another bone in the door...
2	box	You fit the last bone into the recess.
2	box	You place the bone into the last recess on the skeletal door and it fits. All the recesses are filled...
2	box	The door seems to change slightly. Two depictions of skeletal warriors turn their heads towards you. They are alive! The Skeletons wrench themselves free of the door. Stepping out of the door, with grinning teeth they push the huge doors open.
1	action	end
0	section	Look-at or Search Tomb dolmen
1	box	You touch the dolmen, and the ground starts to shake. You hear an unearthly voice booming and you step away from the dolmen in anticipation.
1	action	Nazastarool spawns.
1	line	Nazastarool	I am Nazastarool! Prepare to die!
1	action	Continues after killing Nazastarool.
1	box	You defeat Nazastarool and the corpse falls to the ground. The bones start to move again and soon they reform into a grisly giant skeleton.
1	action	Nazastarool spawns again.
1	line	Nazastarool	Quake in fear, for I am reborn!
1	line	Nazastarool	Your death will be swift.
1	action	Continues after killing Nazastarool.
1	box	You defeat Nazastarool and the skeleton falls to the ground. An ethereal form starts taking shape above the bones and you soon face the vengeful ghost of Nazastarool.
1	action	Nazastarool spawns again.
1	line	Nazastarool	Nazastarool returns with vengeance!
1	line	Nazastarool	Soon you will serve Rashiliyia.
1	action	Continues after killing Nazastarool.
1	box	You hear a disembodied voice fading away into the distance, 'May you perish in the fires of Zamorak's furnace! Rashiliyia's curse is upon you!'
1	box	You see something appear on the dolmen.
1	box	Nazastarool: May you perish in the fires of Zamorak's furnace! Rashiliyia's
1	box	Nazastarool: curse is upon you!
1	action	end
